WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.500
Unseen Foe
Sea Stealth II

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.510
Jonouchi...

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.240
Where are you?

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.200
You're Yugi Muto, right?

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.530
If you want to go any further, you must defeat us.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.880
In a duel, of course.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.990
Rare Hunters...

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.390
Move out of my way!

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:54.100
No.  If we let you through, Marik will punish us.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:54.860
Also...

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.450
If you don't duel us, your friends will be disposed of immediately.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.560
Who's going first?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:05.150
You go first.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.330
Not a chance.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.930
But still...

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.880
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.080
Okay.  One two...

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:13.640
Shoot!

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.240
Again!

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.180
Again!

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.730
You don't always have to play paper.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.760
Right.  Let's keep going.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.420
One two shoot!

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.930
Again!

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:29.830
Knock it off!

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.160
Sorry, Yugi.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.070
But it's not like we can duel you two-on-one.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.570
Then let's have a tag match, you wimps!

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.160
Kaiba!

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.110
I'll team up with Yugi.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.020
A tag match?

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.610
We have the right number of players.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.920
Don't get the wrong idea, Yugi.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:58.180
I created Battle City to destroy the rare card-stealing Ghouls.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.370
I won't let them use these precious cards for evil purposes.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.840
I'm not here to help you or your loser friend.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:12.270
Or maybe you don't need my help because you've acquired a God Card?

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.670
Kaiba...

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.470
This is good for us.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:23.920
If we defeat you both, Marik will think highly of us.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.040
Here we go!

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.080
Duel!

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.240
Bring it on.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:33.430
We'll send you to hell.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.200
You're deluding yourselves if you think you can win.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.240
My turn.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.960
The spell card Pot of Greed.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.580
It lets me draw two cards from my deck.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.520
I summon Lord of D.!

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.650
I use the spell The Flute of Summoning Dragon!

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.950
Two Flutes?

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:12.460
When Lord of D. is faceup, The Flute of Summoning Dragon lets me summon two dragons from my hand.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.200
That means...

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:18.870
Come, Blue-Eyes White Dragons and Hyozanryu!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.900
No way!  Four dragons already?

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.900
The first player can't attack.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.920
I end my turn.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:43.390
Bring it on.  Even though you're weaklings, I won't show any mercy.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.800
Damn!  A monster in defense position!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.500
I end my turn!

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.970
My turn.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.340
I set two cards.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.670
Stay out of this, Yugi!

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.950
I don't want your help.

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.180
What?

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.180
I can handle these wealkings by myself.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.050
Then I'll just watch.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.080
Kuriboh in defense position.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.790
It's your turn.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.300
This isn't going well.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.400
Leave it to me.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:28.670
Even if he has powerful dragons, I have a trap in my hand that will destroy them in an instant.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.180
The Ghouls can copy any rare card.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:42.540
I set one card and a monster in defense position.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:44.150
I end my turn.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.360
Is that a trap or a spell?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.390
It doesn't matter either way.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.200
Be careful, Kaiba.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.900
They're up to something.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.900
Yugi, I told you to stay out of this!

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.130
Kaiba!

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.320
Let me show you.

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:03.380
I have a God, just like you.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.380
Blue-Eyes, become God's power!

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.690
Watch this, Yugi!

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:17.000
Come out, Obelisk!

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.600
What?

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:30.770
This is...

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.510
This is one of the God Cards, Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.580
I tribute two monsters!

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.050
Its effect activates!

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.390
Our defending monsters!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.550
Obelisk attacks!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.770
God Hand Crusher!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.130
You fell for my trap!

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:07.100
Mirror Force!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.340
That lame thing doesn't work against a God!

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:13.450
Go!

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.700
Did you see my God, Yugi?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:31.070
So this is Kaiba's God Card, Obelisk the Tormentor.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.680
Where's Jonouchi?

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:38.770
Damn!

00:07:39.170 --> 00:07:42.510
These weaklings had Puzzle Cards.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.170
This is yours.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.140
I'm going to look for Jonouchi.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.540
Wait!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.680
Stop bugging me!  Now isn't the time!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.370
Mokuba, contact HQ.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:56.700
You're going to look for Jonouchi?

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:02.580
If that loser starts dueling, our systems will detect him.

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:03.690
Kaiba...

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:09.700
But once you save him, we're going to settle things once and for all.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:18.270
So that's the infamous Obelisk.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.450
I've figured that God Card out.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.450
Oh yeah!

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.510
A big haul!

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.790
What are you doing?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.920
That's what I should be saying!

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:43.900
I was catching my lunch, but I'm going to be lunch!

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.700
Who cares about lunch!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.140
This is an aquarium!

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:51.210
Aquarium?

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:53.840
I thought it was a giant fish tank.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.650
You're still stealing from a fish tank!

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.400
What's wrong?

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.890
You have a fever.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.110
There's an important orca show today.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.800
I have to be in it.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.000
You're too sick.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.630
But people are excited to see the show.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:20.640
Okay then!  I'll handle the show!

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:30.200
Yugi's Slifer and Kaiba's Obelisk...  Interesting.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:33.320
But I'll get those two God Cards back soon.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.020
This signal...

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.540
It's the shadow power that controlled Keith.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.390
He's coming this way.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.550
Battle City is unexpectedly helping me achieve my goals.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:50.300
Bakura!

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:54.800
You came to see Battle City too?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.810
Yeah.

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.370
Jonouchi, are you winning?

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:02.600
Yeah.  I have four Puzzle Cards.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.110
I need two more to make the finals.

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:07.150
Wow!

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.750
Huh?  Where's Yugi?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.840
We're looking for him too.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.690
But I'm sure he's winning.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:18.440
Yeah.  He may have already made the finals.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.660
You have no time to waste.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:25.200
Yeah.  Is there anyone worth dueling around here?

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.440
What's wrong?

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.160
What's this?

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.240
It says Ryota.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.680
Kajiki!  That guy!

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.750
I know who I'm dueling next!

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:38.380
Jonouchi!

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:41.840
Hey!  Wait for me!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.620
I have to go meet our new guest.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.500
Where are you, Kajiki?

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.660
Jonouchi, look!

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.670
What is he doing?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.400
Oh yeah!

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.380
What are you doing?

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.280
Hey, Jonouchi!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.880
Long time no see, Jonouchi.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.530
The last time was Duelist Kingdom.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:05.030
Kajiki, you're supposed to duel in the city, not at the aquarium.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:09.580
Due to circumstances, I have to help the show.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.040
What?  But I came here to duel!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.140
You want to duel me?

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:15.360
Bad idea.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.050
You're no match for my Sea Deck.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:19.280
What?

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.780
I only need two more Puzzle Cards to make the finals.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:24.990
Same here!

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.700
Hey, not bad!

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.720
How about helping the show with a duel?

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:32.960
Sounds fun!  I'll do it!

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.970
They're starting something!

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:38.080
It'll be Battle City!  Hooray!

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.200
It's nice to have a crowd.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.210
Jonouchi, we'll wager two Puzzle Cards.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:47.210
The winner goes to the finals.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.010
Fine!  We'll also wager two rare cards!

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:51.940
Let's do this.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:52.450
Yeah!

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.220
Duel!

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:04.760
Do your best, Jonouchi!

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:09.500
If I win this duel, I can keep my promise with Yugi.

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:13.630
I heard he finished second at Duelist Kingdom due to luck.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:17.500
I'll test how good he is.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:21.440
I go first!  I draw!

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:25.880
What was that?

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.520
That dumb showoff!

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.170
I look cool.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.020
Parasite Paracide?

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.250
Oh no!  I forgot to take it out!

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:40.030
Oh wait.  I don't have to panic just because I left it in my deck.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.330
It gave me a lot of trouble.

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:48.770
So I'll now use it to give Kajiki trouble!

00:13:49.700 --> 00:13:51.930
Hmm...  Let's see...

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:56.540
"Flip the card: Put this card faceup in your opponent's deck and shuffle it."

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:58.460
What's taking so long?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.280
Play your turn!

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:01.850
I know!

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.870
Don't tell me that you don't know what cards are in your deck?

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.540
That's not true!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.020
It's all part of my strategy!

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:13.260
Anyway, I need this card to flip faceup.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.530
I set this card in defense position.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.220
Showoff.

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:24.100
I summon Flying Fish!

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:29.680
I don't know your strategy, but I'll still attack!

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.850
All right!  Parasite Paracide!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:37.550
Huh?  Why isn't it infected?

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:42.920
You dummy!  Paracide's Flip Effect only activates when it survives!

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.660
That means...

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:48.400
If it's destroyed, it goes to the graveyard before activating its effect.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.900
What?

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:53.400
Sheesh.  He's failing as usual.

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:55.350
Damn!  My turn.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:57.350
A monster in defense position.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:02.400
His monster likely has high defense points.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.160
He'll use it to summon a superior monster later.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.770
Your strategy is so obvious.  In that case...

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:12.000
My turn!  I set one card!

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:14.520
I end my turn.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.620
All right!  My turn!

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.780
Watch as I draw elegantly-

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.530
Hurry up already!

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.760
Sheesh!  Appreciate my showmanship!

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:25.300
I draw a card.

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:27.030
Prepare yourself, Kajiki!

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:32.570
I tribute a monster to summon Garoozis!

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.860
I activate a trap card!

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.140
Torrential Tribute!

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:46.390
I've never met such a weak duelist.

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:59.800
Yugi, you will suffer greatly when I turn your friend into my puppet.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:12.780
Who are you?

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:17.290
The Millennium Ring.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:21.660
Give me your Millennium Item.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.220
I'll erase anyone who interferes with my plans.

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:30.230
I see.  You're collecting the Millennium Items.

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:31.460
Why?

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:32.970
Isn't it obvious?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:35.970
In a secret Egyptian temple...

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:42.370
...I'll place the seven Items in the Tablet of the Pharaoh's Memories to open the door of shadows.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:46.480
I'll acquire the evil power that was sealed away.

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.850
Only the gravekeepers know about this, so how does he know?

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:59.430
But he doesn't know that the seven Millennium Items aren't enough to open the door of shadows.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:05.130
That secret is carved on my back.

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:07.300
My name is Marik.

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.440
I'm Bakura.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:12.610
Bakura, I have no interest in the Millennium Items.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.840
I only care about killing the nameless Pharaoh.

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:21.350
After I kill him, this Millennium Rod is a piece of junk to me.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.730
This guy...

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:24.560
I have a proposition.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:30.590
If you help me defeat Yugi, I'll let you have this after it's over.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.350
A proposition?

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:37.360
I told you to give me the Millennium Item.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.400
I have my own reasons.

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:45.610
I can't let you have this until I finish Yugi.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:51.110
Then let's fight with our shadow powers.  Millennium Rod vs Millennium Ring.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.110
Let's do it.

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.400
My turn!

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.670
Flying Fish attacks you directly!

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:04.960
Torpedo Charge!

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:10.900
Jonouchi!

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.900
I set a card and end my turn.

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.250
I'm disappointed, Jonouchi!

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:20.920
You were goofing off in this duel!

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:22.640
What?  Goofing off?

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:27.000
Yeah.  No matter the opponent, I fight with all my strength.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.880
That's how I show respect!

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.570
It's the same when I'm out at sea.

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:35.890
I give my all to catch the smallest fish!

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:40.130
If I don't, I'll be the one who gets swallowed up!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:47.400
I entered the tournament because I need the prize money to replace the boat I lost!

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:52.170
That's why I never slack off!

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:57.610
Even the ocean is looking forward to the day when it can battle me again!

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.450
Who I want to battle...

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.820
My ocean is...

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:09.020
Kajiki, there's someone I want to battle too.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.600
I don't want to have regrets later.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:14.590
I'll duel with all my might!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.830
Bring it on, Jonouchi!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.950
Do your best, Jonouchi!

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.340
Keep calm.

00:19:24.340 --> 00:19:26.570
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:30.100
Alligator's Sword in attack position!

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.200
And I set two cards.

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.320
I end my turn!

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.500
It's harder to attack him than before.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:45.200
Because I sense your dueling spirit, Jonouchi!

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:48.730
But my spirit is stronger!

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.460
My turn!

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:55.930
I tribute Flying Fish to summon Amphibian Beast!

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:59.570
2400 attack points?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:02.460
Here I go!  Amphibian Beast attacks!

00:20:02.460 --> 00:20:03.810
Sea Claw!

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.950
I activate my set card!

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.420
What?  The monster entered the box?

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:18.890
Can you tell where it's hiding?

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.270
Not good enough, Jonouchi.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:23.630
Did you forget I had this card?

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.860
The Field Card Umi!

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:34.270
Fairy Box is underwater!

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:38.500
Alligator's Sword can't breathe underwater.

00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.050
Found it!  Go!

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.940
I activate a spell card!

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.420
Skull Dice!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:52.390
Your monster loses attack points depending on what I roll.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.140
Nice!  Our life points are almost equal!

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:05.500
Not bad.  You're making things interesting.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:10.840
But Jonouchi, you don't know how dangerous the ocean can be.

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:16.680
A first-rate fisherman lures his prey into his territory for a sure catch.

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:25.150
Jonouchi, you're already caught in my net.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:31.430
I'll show you my strategy for victory known as Sea Stealth II!

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:46.820
Due to the Umi Field, all of Kajiki's monsters are hiding underwater.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.700
It's your chance to attack Kajiki directly!

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:53.400
What?  The water rose and blocked the attack?

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:57.550
Be careful, Jonouchi!  Something is attacking from under the ocean!

00:21:57.550 --> 00:22:01.590
What?  That monster is the double of Kajiki's father?

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:04.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
The Legendary Fisherman

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.420
Duel, standby!

00:22:20.930 --> 00:22:25.430
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.230 --> 00:22:30.800
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:40.460
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:51.970
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:59.500
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:04.770
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.330 --> 00:23:09.850
Will never change

00:23:10.540 --> 00:23:15.120
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:20.350
To be who I am

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:25.590
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:30.270
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.270 --> 00:23:33.230
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:40.340
From now until forever...
